WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.974
Score every alternative against the same scenarios,
using shared rating anchors and evidence.

00:00:05.974 --> 00:00:09.058
Multiply each rating by its leaf weight and add.

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:15.353
In our invented example, A scores about one point
nine five eight three and B about one point nine

00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:16.316
three zero six.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.794
The difference is tiny.

00:00:17.794 --> 00:00:23.704
Unknown evidence must remain visible, and mandatory
requirements must be checked separately.

00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:26.307
A useful decision model can be challenged.

00:00:26.307 --> 00:00:31.762
Move Availability above Performance and our shared
platform becomes the stronger option.

00:00:31.762 --> 00:00:36.472
Reduce a weakly supported rating and the original
narrow lead may disappear.

00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:41.059
This tells the team what to test and which
stakeholder assumptions matter.

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:46.079
Revisit the framework during planning cycles,
keeping the rationale and evidence.

00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:49.381
QODA also gives technical debt a concrete meaning.

00:00:49.381 --> 00:00:52.527
A shortcut buys time by accepting a quality gap.

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:56.591
The time saved is not necessarily the future
repayment effort.

00:00:56.591 --> 00:01:02.949
Compare the actual and desired designs against
current scenarios, identify the important gaps and

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:05.833
estimate the engineering work to close them.

00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:08.717
Revisit the target as business needs change.

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:12.322
A weighted quality gap is not a unit of developer
time.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:16.398
Finish with a decision record that another team can
audit.

00:01:16.398 --> 00:01:22.724
Include the context, quality tree, scenarios,
rankings, path weights, evidence, scores and

00:01:22.724 --> 00:01:24.059
sensitivity checks.

00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:27.644
Use the lab to reproduce and challenge the example.

00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:31.299
Then apply the method to a new notification service.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:36.570
The goal is a transparent, revisable argument, not
merely a winning number.
